ntersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074138 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec4c6de4-a7fd-5851-accd-9c5156477afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 2x - 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071026} {:answer/id #uuid "f81e9c0d-0f7f-5808-ae52-8f03e0039400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071027} {:answer/id #uuid "0e89162b-dfe2-5744-9796-d0f1635ed693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 3x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071028} {:answer/id #uuid "49a90275-fbc9-561c-b080-6352f5ee175a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, x + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071029} {:answer/id #uuid "677e1be5-b5d0-5254-975c-3550e4fc1853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 3x - 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071030}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea64686-cfe1-5de1-94d2-5c5e04adbf93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071025}] :question/id #uuid "cb252b96-4a13-53c2-bed5-4b7dd119cf7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-25524" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9x - 3y &= -6 \\\\[6pt]\n3x - y &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ee3752b-c151-5d7c-b459-269e7a440470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529275} {:answer/id #uuid "ad343ca9-8ee8-59ee-8492-d87f4e5767a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529312} {:answer/id #uuid "afaa3c2f-68a9-5e46-b525-4af2bb7fbccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad343ca9-8ee8-59ee-8492-d87f4e5767a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529312} :answer-field/id #uuid "431a38a6-e58c-5853-ad1f-a6fc6bb01e65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17e3609b-1396-5685-843a-74d27fdadf0f" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x + y &=6 \\\\ x - 2y &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $2$, then we will get a $2x$ term that can cancel with the $-2x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x + y &=6 \\\\ x - 2y &=6 && \\mid \\cdot (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, the $x$ terms cancel, and we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x + y &= 6 \\\\\n2x - 4y &= 12 \\\\\n-3y &= (6 + 12) \\\\\n-3y &= 18 \\\\\ny &= -6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x + (1)(-6) &= 6 \\\\\n-2x &= 12 \\\\\nx &= -6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system has *a single solution*, $(-6,-6)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529263 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71a19f9f-c97f-5b22-a3fb-3ddd84649033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529285} {:answer/id #uuid "7968a19d-81e4-508f-8ec6-11e1b7db0381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529288} {:answer/id #uuid "cd558f16-0c95-5532-85ce-16a34dea6a67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7968a19d-81e4-508f-8ec6-11e1b7db0381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529288} :answer-field/id #uuid "a88aecce-0e48-579b-8ac8-fffb289b1a69" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "22c76199-015b-5355-8da5-51b3e4eb6386" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y + 2x + 4 &=0 \\\\ 4y - 4x + 9 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nFirst, rearrange each equation to put the variable terms on the left and the constant on the right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + y &= -4 \\\\\n-4x + 4y &= -9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $4x$ term that can cancel with the $-4x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x + y &=-4 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ -4x + 4y &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, the $x$ terms cancel, and we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x + 2y &= -8 \\\\\n-4x + 4y &= -9 \\\\\n6y &= (-8 - 9) \\\\\n6y &= -17 \\\\\ny &= - \\frac{17}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + (1)\\left(- \\frac{17}{6}\\right) &= -4 \\\\\n2x &= - \\frac{7}{6} \\\\\nx &= - \\frac{7}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system has *a single solution*, $(- \\frac{7}{12},- \\frac{17}{6})$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "344db828-cf79-52e5-a777-8ab84b874966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529268} {:answer/id #uuid "95396471-ccc2-5ee9-a8d6-43bc15e844c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529298} {:answer/id #uuid "dcdd0cde-b36f-54e5-a018-7db85e9b5a1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "344db828-cf79-52e5-a777-8ab84b874966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529268} :answer-field/id #uuid "65b4752f-c56d-5617-8e96-0a2d7a4fd12a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "27a6ba63-3c85-5feb-bfac-b122a5e9f9a3" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x + 4y &=-9 \\\\ 2x - y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $2$, then we will get a $4x$ term that can cancel with the $-4x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x + 4y &=-9 \\\\ 2x - y &=-4 && \\mid \\cdot (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, the $x$ terms cancel, and we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x + 4y &= -9 \\\\\n4x - 2y &= -8 \\\\\n2y &= (-9 - 8) \\\\\n2y &= -17 \\\\\ny &= - \\frac{17}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x + (4)\\left(- \\frac{17}{2}\\right) &= -9 \\\\\n-4x &= 25 \\\\\nx &= - \\frac{25}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system has *a single solution*, $(- \\frac{25}{4},- \\frac{17}{2})$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529266 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fbdb8ad-267a-57e1-90cb-804824fd158a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529259} {:answer/id #uuid "31e0880c-27b5-5a13-87e6-3705af860da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529267} {:answer/id #uuid "8c8210fd-75fb-5771-887f-af1bb8ec8244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529295 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186656365}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c8210fd-75fb-5771-887f-af1bb8ec8244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529295} :answer-field/id #uuid "6093ddec-b3cd-5a0b-8a78-bde2db784aa4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "31a5b8b3-2787-5aca-9212-729c0bca425f" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y + 2x + 2 &=0 \\\\ 4y + 8x + 8 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nFirst, rearrange each equation to put the variable terms on the left and the constant on the right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + y &= -2 \\\\\n8x + 4y &= -8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $-4$, then we will get a $-8x$ term that can cancel with the $8x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x + y &=-2 && \\mid \\cdot (-4) \\\\ 8x + 4y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x - 4y &= 8 \\\\\n8x + 4y &= -8 \\\\\n0 &= (8 - 8) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=0$ is *always true*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *infinitely many solutions*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193a9776-9522-59e8-93fb-4b3bab86a5ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529262} {:answer/id #uuid "ac9317b7-c236-5932-99c1-b650c3ecfd60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529311 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186656363}]} {:answer/id #uuid "ece64018-7584-599e-8625-2cc9d1912aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ece64018-7584-599e-8625-2cc9d1912aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529327} :answer-field/id #uuid "e77cb455-ca55-5d77-ab3a-caef6fb910d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45038183-ddb8-5749-92cf-2124aeefd6a9" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x + y &=2 \\\\ 4x + 2y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2$, then we will get a $-4x$ term that can cancel with the $4x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x + y &=2 && \\mid \\cdot (-2) \\\\ 4x + 2y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x - 2y &= -4 \\\\\n4x + 2y &= 5 \\\\\n0 &= (-4 + 5) \\\\\n0 &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=1$ is *always false*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *no solutions*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a6a9c04-4483-5b31-88cd-fdc0d4f8dfab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529273} {:answer/id #uuid "6532299d-7242-529d-b584-f2d02d122b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529280} {:answer/id #uuid "a3bb91a8-f370-546d-8650-fc4b5ac0f2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3bb91a8-f370-546d-8650-fc4b5ac0f2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529304} :answer-field/id #uuid "571d0d37-8178-57f9-8598-a1a4ba418722" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6df7ea41-de66-50d4-b68f-ac8978094097" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y - 3x + 1 &=0 \\\\ -3y - 6x - 8 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nFirst, rearrange each equation to put the variable terms on the left and the constant on the right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + y &= -1 \\\\\n-6x - 3y &= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2$, then we will get a $6x$ term that can cancel with the $-6x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x + y &=-1 && \\mid \\cdot (-2) \\\\ -6x - 3y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, the $x$ terms cancel, and we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x - 2y &= 2 \\\\\n-6x - 3y &= 8 \\\\\n-5y &= (2 + 8) \\\\\n-5y &= 10 \\\\\ny &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + (1)(-2) &= -1 \\\\\n-3x &= 1 \\\\\nx &= - \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system has *a single solution*, $(- \\frac{1}{3},-2)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46de5fcd-a47b-5970-9703-3a33b936c273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529272} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4a900e-af83-5010-a4eb-550d23e0386f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529302} {:answer/id #uuid "c4bc71c3-edaf-56da-873d-7ff9f6b2544c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f4a900e-af83-5010-a4eb-550d23e0386f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529302} :answer-field/id #uuid "defa217b-2cb1-5a93-8730-0a2de2c923fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7b1e2d9a-93ed-5edd-af89-794105a0828b" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x - 3y &=10 \\\\ 4x - 2y &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2$, then we will get a $-4x$ term that can cancel with the $4x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x - 3y &=10 && \\text{multiply by } -2 \\\\ 4x - 2y &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, the $x$ terms cancel, and we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x + 6y &= -20 \\\\\n4x - 2y &= 12 \\\\\n4y &= (-20 + 12) \\\\\n4y &= -8 \\\\\ny &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + (-3)(-2) &= 10 \\\\\n2x &= 4 \\\\\nx &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system has *a single solution*, $(2,-2)$.\n\nThe corresponding lines intersect at exactly one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d893df7-d857-5192-90ce-47a99d5c6bf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529274} {:answer/id #uuid "60bc4533-01cd-595e-9372-f185d24aa9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529279} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce6a4fc-25b3-542c-aed5-70e5fdd4a918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d893df7-d857-5192-90ce-47a99d5c6bf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529274} :answer-field/id #uuid "7aa9bc9c-c996-5d30-bb22-558885c83ec4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "878a99ca-9540-5195-b258-8e98913442f4" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x - y &=-2 \\\\ 8x - 4y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $-4$, then we will get a $-8x$ term that can cancel with the $8x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x - y &=-2 && \\mid \\cdot (-4) \\\\ 8x - 4y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 4y &= 8 \\\\\n8x - 4y &= -8 \\\\\n0 &= (8 - 8) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=0$ is *always true*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *infinitely many solutions*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aedf24db-2200-5c34-82c8-69e05734e790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529313} {:answer/id #uuid "d688773d-636f-5a54-b4ee-355c9f396330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529321} {:answer/id #uuid "f2dee143-55db-5cf5-83a5-24cd943aae58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2dee143-55db-5cf5-83a5-24cd943aae58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529329} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5171cd4-7721-5fe2-926b-265c33c00b33" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88e09a62-e93a-583d-86c5-5caff22bdcbd" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x + 2y &=0 \\\\ -3x + 5y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $2$, then we will get a $-6x$ term that can cancel with the $6x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x + 2y &=0 \\\\ -3x + 5y &=-2 && \\text{multiply by } 2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, the $x$ terms cancel, and we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x + 2y &= 0 \\\\\n-6x + 10y &= -4 \\\\\n12y &= (0 - 4) \\\\\n12y &= -4 \\\\\ny &= - \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x + (2)\\left(- \\frac{1}{3}\\right) &= 0 \\\\\n6x &= \\frac{2}{3} \\\\\nx &= \\frac{1}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system has *a single solution*, $(\\frac{1}{9},- \\frac{1}{3})$.\n\nThe corresponding lines intersect at exactly one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26412d41-7859-567a-8d0b-616fdfaae78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529264} {:answer/id #uuid "7ebeb28b-d7e8-58ed-a1ac-c3da8dc6de13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529291 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574059}]} {:answer/id #uuid "ede703e4-312f-541c-9af9-a20919d7afce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ebeb28b-d7e8-58ed-a1ac-c3da8dc6de13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529291} :answer-field/id #uuid "43939bab-211c-5b1e-9dcd-127b5f8c732a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a7d7084c-4c14-5312-a22d-dc6fe1986a2c" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x - y &=8 \\\\ 6x + 2y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $-6x$ term that can cancel with the $6x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x - y &=8 && \\text{multiply by } 2 \\\\ 6x + 2y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-6x - 2y &= 16 \\\\\n6x + 2y &= -12 \\\\\n0 &= (16 - 12) \\\\\n0 &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=4$ is *always false*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *no solutions*.\n\nThe corresponding lines are parallel and do not intersect."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d5289c2-ae65-5854-8e71-5b033554cd5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529258} {:answer/id #uuid "81a01f27-1606-571b-a96b-5a5040320fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529292} {:answer/id #uuid "9d492ab7-1bb8-5fc1-8c03-1d65e9d953d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d492ab7-1bb8-5fc1-8c03-1d65e9d953d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529301} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2ae9c90-b5af-556d-b9c0-2e84879f0db0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a81cacd7-ddb8-5f18-91b0-0d7142c96649" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y - 3x - 4 &=0 \\\\ -2y + 12x + 10 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nFirst, rearrange each equation to put the variable terms on the left and the constant on the right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + y &= 4 \\\\\n12x - 2y &= -10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $4$, then we will get a $-12x$ term that can cancel with the $12x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x + y &=4 && \\mid \\cdot (4) \\\\ 12x - 2y &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, the $x$ terms cancel, and we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x + 4y &= 16 \\\\\n12x - 2y &= -10 \\\\\n2y &= (16 - 10) \\\\\n2y &= 6 \\\\\ny &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + (1)(3) &= 4 \\\\\n-3x &= 1 \\\\\nx &= - \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system has *a single solution*, $(- \\frac{1}{3},3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02e4adab-f965-574b-b1b2-5412f0ac4030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529257} {:answer/id #uuid "174a23c4-66b4-574b-ab16-58c635103256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529260} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf0dc60-cd74-50bb-bbf6-488567b34736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "174a23c4-66b4-574b-ab16-58c635103256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529260} :answer-field/id #uuid "da21e2ad-53b7-539d-8fc6-d73ab8480a65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a93a39cc-73b6-5e4b-80a4-1282a4d64974" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y + 3x + 6 &=0 \\\\ -4y - 12x - 26 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nFirst, rearrange each equation to put the variable terms on the left and the constant on the right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x + y &= -6 \\\\\n-12x - 4y &= 26\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $4$, then we will get a $12x$ term that can cancel with the $-12x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x + y &=-6 && \\mid \\cdot (4) \\\\ -12x - 4y &=26\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12x + 4y &= -24 \\\\\n-12x - 4y &= 26 \\\\\n0 &= (-24 + 26) \\\\\n0 &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=2$ is *always false*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *no solutions*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529316 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72bba841-9529-5598-b921-f90b8dffbe5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529286} {:answer/id #uuid "b27078db-ea72-5bd8-9115-2ea5343e2f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529315} {:answer/id #uuid "f96540d7-0eb1-5d77-a5ce-3fa81473a266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b27078db-ea72-5bd8-9115-2ea5343e2f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529315} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c1fbec3-c232-5078-a580-2f08b5aa37e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0b2af50-0676-5686-aa21-aed280aaa725" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x - 5y &=-12 \\\\ 2x - 6y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $-2x$ term that can cancel with the $2x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x - 5y &=-12 && \\text{multiply by } 2 \\\\ 2x - 6y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, the $x$ terms cancel, and we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 10y &= -24 \\\\\n2x - 6y &= -4 \\\\\n-16y &= (-24 - 4) \\\\\n-16y &= -28 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{7}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x + (-5)\\left(\\frac{7}{4}\\right) &= -12 \\\\\n-x &= - \\frac{13}{4} \\\\\nx &= \\frac{13}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system has *a single solution*, $(\\frac{13}{4},\\frac{7}{4})$.\n\nThe corresponding lines intersect at exactly one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f5d6e30-8e43-5909-9e9a-3a9af82fd1e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529297 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574180}]} {:answer/id #uuid "9c1af611-f1dc-57a7-b4ff-1cd30b5d58d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529300} {:answer/id #uuid "a979b510-0d7a-5573-bce5-5f77d85dffa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f5d6e30-8e43-5909-9e9a-3a9af82fd1e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529297} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eaf5b55-2fa9-5c35-a346-66798bb8f61b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5970b8b-793c-585b-9c66-c8937f9714fc" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 3y &=-6 \\\\ 4x - y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $-4$, then we will get a $-4x$ term that can cancel with the $4x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 3y &=-6 && \\mid \\cdot (-4) \\\\ 4x - y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, the $x$ terms cancel, and we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x + 12y &= 24 \\\\\n4x - y &= -12 \\\\\n11y &= (24 - 12) \\\\\n11y &= 12 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{12}{11}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx + (-3)\\left(\\frac{12}{11}\\right) &= -6 \\\\\nx &= - \\frac{30}{11} \\\\\nx &= - \\frac{30}{11}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system has *a single solution*, $(- \\frac{30}{11},\\frac{12}{11})$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fb0b299-f16e-54c2-a393-40d6eef9a51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529276} {:answer/id #uuid "97b495fd-486c-5329-aea6-b7fef9362dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529299} {:answer/id #uuid "a66f4ab0-02ae-5f53-884d-c689e9f292e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529305 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186656361}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a66f4ab0-02ae-5f53-884d-c689e9f292e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529305} :answer-field/id #uuid "766ff9b6-bfc6-59ad-af1f-7918abd24f91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d4bc3484-819e-515d-b935-6bb887858fab" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x - 2y &=8 \\\\ 2x - y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $-2$, then we will get a $-4x$ term that can cancel with the $4x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x - 2y &=8 \\\\ 2x - y &=4 && \\text{multiply by } -2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 2y &= 8 \\\\\n-4x + 2y &= -8 \\\\\n0 &= (8 - 8) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=0$ is *always true*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nThe corresponding lines coincide."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "296b4bc1-fdc9-57c7-8838-c40039d81743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -4x + 8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542454} {:answer/id #uuid "511c3e07-7b86-5d35-b593-e086d056c9e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{1}{4}x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542467} {:answer/id #uuid "72f94d33-8b49-509e-9f3b-feef2915a2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542474} {:answer/id #uuid "993d12f6-8426-5581-93dc-e143dd73cada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 4x + 8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542483} {:answer/id #uuid "d647aaba-1ddd-551d-acf3-4af820d6199d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -4x - 8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "296b4bc1-fdc9-57c7-8838-c40039d81743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -4x + 8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542454} :answer-field/id #uuid "a496eb60-5280-58e8-963e-50a6d3c4762a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "088c2bc7-791c-5d33-989e-2db1686f3a99" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x + y &= 8 \\\\[6pt]\n-8x - 2y &= -16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x + y &=8 \\\\ -8x - 2y &=-16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $8x$ term that can cancel with the $-8x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x + y &=8 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ -8x - 2y &=-16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8x + 2y &= 16 \\\\\n-8x - 2y &= -16 \\\\\n0 &= (16 - 16) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x + y &= 8 \\\\\ny &= 8 - 4x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{8 - 4x}{1} \\\\\ny &= 8 - 4x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,8 - 4x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76fe33fa-ce38-5b2f-ae1b-8a6fb1ff5121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{4}x + \\frac{3}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542475} {:answer/id #uuid "c99c9047-694a-52fb-90a1-920055039ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{4}x - \\frac{3}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542494} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2b29a2-d8c3-5c8b-ab33-30360a9a3463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{1}{4}x - \\frac{3}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542495} {:answer/id #uuid "e3aad1d2-6e42-5eec-9dca-2cec7a5ae0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 4x + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542503} {:answer/id #uuid "ff7fd8bf-f7d2-584f-a1df-b2f38182412f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{3}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c99c9047-694a-52fb-90a1-920055039ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{4}x - \\frac{3}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542494} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bf547af-6a9e-5a7b-a100-571509ee17b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0b630dc7-b870-5e2b-85ac-37faee98683d" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx - 4y &= 3 \\\\[6pt]\n-4x + 16y &= -12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 4y &=3 \\\\ -4x + 16y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $4$, then we will get a $4x$ term that can cancel with the $-4x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 4y &=3 && \\mid \\cdot (4) \\\\ -4x + 16y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 16y &= 12 \\\\\n-4x + 16y &= -12 \\\\\n0 &= (12 - 12) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx - 4y &= 3 \\\\\n-4y &= 3 - x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{3 - x}{-4} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{3}{4} + \\frac{1}{4}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,-\\frac{3}{4} + \\frac{1}{4}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a28e7ec-e71a-5f77-bd2b-aee856b5039c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 2x + 10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542444} {:answer/id #uuid "1bbc4b58-5af2-531c-9f2a-e95c4507960c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{2}x - 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542446} {:answer/id #uuid "2528686b-8db2-507f-9663-1012eeb1fbf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542453} {:answer/id #uuid "6ae1c305-4510-5421-8776-69299ea2148b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{1}{2}x - 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542473} {:answer/id #uuid "ea2d669d-5e96-546b-9cbb-0faab3e8ff37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{2}x + 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bbc4b58-5af2-531c-9f2a-e95c4507960c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{2}x - 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542446} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f8a0b2e-30d5-55be-9faa-704ff5f10ec6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "111bc200-5458-59e4-8bff-0e4766f93526" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx - 2y &= 10 \\\\[6pt]\n3x - 6y &= 30\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 2y &=10 \\\\ 3x - 6y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then we will get a $-3x$ term that can cancel with the $3x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 2y &=10 && \\mid \\cdot (-3) \\\\ 3x - 6y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + 6y &= -30 \\\\\n3x - 6y &= 30 \\\\\n0 &= (-30 + 30) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx - 2y &= 10 \\\\\n-2y &= 10 - x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{10 - x}{-2} \\\\\ny &= -5 + \\frac{1}{2}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,-5 + \\frac{1}{2}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "216e4d60-197f-5cc4-a6a9-1f0aa4798fd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542451} {:answer/id #uuid "677f2479-49ce-5f74-a164-ff8f5c291ff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -2x - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542472} {:answer/id #uuid "925e9f49-23ce-555d-bfa2-ceaec62717c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 2x + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542481} {:answer/id #uuid "b93fa3dc-f26f-535d-b424-a60e27978200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 2x - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542490 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186656362}]} {:answer/id #uuid "f9ce12fe-1da9-5977-a390-7992e5b701d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b93fa3dc-f26f-535d-b424-a60e27978200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 2x - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542490} :answer-field/id #uuid "db9b9d32-7ef3-5e9b-8814-93028e12c1b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1dff70b5-3044-54d1-b535-83ffa052215f" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - y &= 1 \\\\[6pt]\n-4x + 2y &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x - y &=1 \\\\ -4x + 2y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $4x$ term that can cancel with the $-4x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x - y &=1 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ -4x + 2y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 2y &= 2 \\\\\n-4x + 2y &= -2 \\\\\n0 &= (2 - 2) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - y &= 1 \\\\\n-y &= 1 - 2x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{1 - 2x}{-1} \\\\\ny &= -1 + 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,-1 + 2x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "329c8c6c-64c9-53b9-abcb-a88c8eeeb32e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "329c8c6c-64c9-53b9-abcb-a88c8eeeb32e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542458} :answer-field/id #uuid "d774ba4e-5e04-5b25-ac80-8bb3704ee4df" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542498}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23da70bf-d870-5a7b-895c-27d6ebda3437" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - y &= -6 \\\\[6pt]\n6x - 3y &= -18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $x$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(x,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x - y &=-6 \\\\ 6x - 3y &=-18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then we will get a $-6x$ term that can cancel with the $6x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x - y &=-6 && \\mid \\cdot (-3) \\\\ 6x - 3y &=-18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-6x + 3y &= 18 \\\\\n6x - 3y &= -18 \\\\\n0 &= (18 - 18) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - y &= -6 \\\\\n-y &= -6 - 2x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-6 - 2x}{-1} \\\\\ny &= 6 + 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,6 + 2x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b794602-b4c5-54ab-8bfc-db1e61594521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + \\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b794602-b4c5-54ab-8bfc-db1e61594521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + \\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542479} :answer-field/id #uuid "337c5621-421b-56d4-95de-5c351f0f1ad9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e38b0b3-85f1-537d-9bdc-738a5616e813" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 2y &= -11 \\\\[6pt]\n8x - 4y &= -22\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $x$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(x,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x - 2y &=-11 \\\\ 8x - 4y &=-22\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2$, then we will get a $-8x$ term that can cancel with the $8x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x - 2y &=-11 && \\mid \\cdot (-2) \\\\ 8x - 4y &=-22\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 4y &= 22 \\\\\n8x - 4y &= -22 \\\\\n0 &= (22 - 22) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 2y &= -11 \\\\\n-2y &= -11 - 4x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-11 - 4x}{-2} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{11}{2} + 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,\\frac{11}{2} + 2x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1265d20a-0e86-57c1-9549-b3dffb34e245" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}x - \\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542443} {:answer/id #uuid "d4c47599-772d-4df0-ba90-27dffe08fede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12x-6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574774 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574773}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1265d20a-0e86-57c1-9549-b3dffb34e245" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}x - \\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542443} :answer-field/id #uuid "0eef6127-aaa5-5be2-ac0e-d2adcd5bbbc7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "48520d96-a4e1-575b-9ec9-8c8c3ed1fafc" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x + 5y &= -6 \\\\[6pt]\n24x - 10y &= 12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $x$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(x,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-12x + 5y &=-6 \\\\ 24x - 10y &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $-24x$ term that can cancel with the $24x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-12x + 5y &=-6 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ 24x - 10y &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-24x + 10y &= -12 \\\\\n24x - 10y &= 12 \\\\\n0 &= (-12 + 12) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x + 5y &= -6 \\\\\n5y &= -6 + 12x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-6 + 12x}{5} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{6}{5} + \\frac{12}{5}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,-\\frac{6}{5} + \\frac{12}{5}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542470 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4830ac95-7dc9-5c52-9bdb-fa5c81554b07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -4x + 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542464} {:answer/id #uuid "59e2aa79-4c55-547b-90bf-a161e58917b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{1}{4}x - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542469} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8e8497-f8a2-5256-b0c3-49b354163e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{4}x + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542487} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c78b75-34eb-5180-b93a-45a32364f55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{1}{4}x + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542493} {:answer/id #uuid "e238b8ec-01f6-516b-b4d3-05d0921577b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6c78b75-34eb-5180-b93a-45a32364f55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{1}{4}x + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542493} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ade77da-f05d-59b2-a201-6a199f319be8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5cb1d607-78ca-599f-a42f-6cb360fcbf56" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x - 4y &= -4 \\\\[6pt]\n2x + 8y &= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x - 4y &=-4 \\\\ 2x + 8y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $-2x$ term that can cancel with the $2x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x - 4y &=-4 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ 2x + 8y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 8y &= -8 \\\\\n2x + 8y &= 8 \\\\\n0 &= (-8 + 8) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x - 4y &= -4 \\\\\n-4y &= -4 + x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-4 + x}{-4} \\\\\ny &= 1 - \\frac{1}{4}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,1 - \\frac{1}{4}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32ec9eaf-8a8c-5485-9397-f4080cccdb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{2}{7}x - \\frac{6}{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542459} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc42961-0c2f-541f-bb32-0b326bb279c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{7}{2}x + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542461} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab9055c-41fa-52d4-98cc-67b4d8dd46ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542484} {:answer/id #uuid "e29a0d02-5cca-5ff8-bf75-9db725841961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{7}{2}x - 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542502} {:answer/id #uuid "f097021f-ff70-5357-a6ad-89cefc4a73f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{7}{2}x + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dc42961-0c2f-541f-bb32-0b326bb279c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{7}{2}x + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542461} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffc4aaed-af07-5113-8443-30d9a263ac17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ab21255-f04c-59e1-a7a8-fd7625364758" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-7x + 2y &= 6 \\\\[6pt]\n-21x + 6y &= 18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-7x + 2y &=6 \\\\ -21x + 6y &=18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then we will get a $21x$ term that can cancel with the $-21x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-7x + 2y &=6 && \\mid \\cdot (-3) \\\\ -21x + 6y &=18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n21x - 6y &= -18 \\\\\n-21x + 6y &= 18 \\\\\n0 &= (-18 + 18) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-7x + 2y &= 6 \\\\\n2y &= 6 + 7x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{6 + 7x}{2} \\\\\ny &= 3 + \\frac{7}{2}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,3 + \\frac{7}{2}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0473f996-4e92-58c5-bd48-4ace42741c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}x + \\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0473f996-4e92-58c5-bd48-4ace42741c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}x + \\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542433} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e20b028-6414-53a2-a73b-b3e227d7d3fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7cd05dfa-1d47-5a9e-9f5f-9a75d2347390" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 3y &= 10 \\\\[6pt]\n21x + 9y &= 30\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $x$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(x,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 3y &=10 \\\\ 21x + 9y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then we will get a $-21x$ term that can cancel with the $21x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 3y &=10 && \\mid \\cdot (-3) \\\\ 21x + 9y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-21x - 9y &= -30 \\\\\n21x + 9y &= 30 \\\\\n0 &= (-30 + 30) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 3y &= 10 \\\\\n3y &= 10 - 7x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{10 - 7x}{3} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{10}{3} - \\frac{7}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,\\frac{10}{3} - \\frac{7}{3}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fa567d4-0454-5e1f-a013-55cfb13bce47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{8}{5}x - \\frac{9}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542449} {:answer/id #uuid "5496138f-4940-59c9-8cfa-4bf807aed2e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{9}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542468} {:answer/id #uuid "65af1755-d621-5206-b9fe-ee7a32a7810b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{5}{8}x + \\frac{9}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542471} {:answer/id #uuid "b130be71-e990-5ee1-afcd-2de31bdb9cb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{8}{5}x + \\frac{9}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542488} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe07f49-e72f-5982-8433-a4f48f9fa695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{8}{5}x - \\frac{9}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fa567d4-0454-5e1f-a013-55cfb13bce47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{8}{5}x - \\frac{9}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542449} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2f7f9e0-a02a-57ec-baf6-911d39f91d52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b9708e75-cf57-54fa-8a86-d6a41661f004" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 5y &= -9 \\\\[6pt]\n16x - 10y &= 18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-8x + 5y &=-9 \\\\ 16x - 10y &=18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $-16x$ term that can cancel with the $16x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-8x + 5y &=-9 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ 16x - 10y &=18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-16x + 10y &= -18 \\\\\n16x - 10y &= 18 \\\\\n0 &= (-18 + 18) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 5y &= -9 \\\\\n5y &= -9 + 8x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-9 + 8x}{5} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{9}{5} + \\frac{8}{5}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,-\\frac{9}{5} + \\frac{8}{5}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c60e70b-96f8-5431-90cd-a6ae562c2fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{6}x + \\frac{2}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542437} {:answer/id #uuid "0e35757a-2c57-5eb8-9b8e-33ffed7823b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 6x - 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542438} {:answer/id #uuid "1cef499e-0ec5-53e4-97d9-a3772813f69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 6x + 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542447} {:answer/id #uuid "4320905f-2597-5dbe-b58d-bb716941c26e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -6x - 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542463} {:answer/id #uuid "49b76269-cc41-593b-a5e2-31e2fd0a943a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e35757a-2c57-5eb8-9b8e-33ffed7823b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 6x - 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542438} :answer-field/id #uuid "10860ce5-13d5-5537-a83d-c826703c2441" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef3faa80-f6ae-5cf6-8c47-c5a225be4ccd" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x - y &= 4 \\\\[6pt]\n-24x + 4y &= -16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x - y &=4 \\\\ -24x + 4y &=-16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $4$, then we will get a $24x$ term that can cancel with the $-24x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x - y &=4 && \\mid \\cdot (4) \\\\ -24x + 4y &=-16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n24x - 4y &= 16 \\\\\n-24x + 4y &= -16 \\\\\n0 &= (16 - 16) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x - y &= 4 \\\\\n-y &= 4 - 6x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4 - 6x}{-1} \\\\\ny &= -4 + 6x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,-4 + 6x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cac595a2-a76f-5528-90a3-5b43bb6b6c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}x + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542496} {:answer/id #uuid "df428421-e8d1-4b41-a517-4bec76a6280f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10-7t}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574812} {:answer/id #uuid "860afaa9-8a2a-53c7-b62d-ad1da456ad5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10-7x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574865 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574775}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cac595a2-a76f-5528-90a3-5b43bb6b6c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}x + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542496} :answer-field/id #uuid "0052794e-29d0-5a14-847c-4f8656980f5a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2d5e6d3-70ba-56f0-872c-ec4406eeabb5" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 2y &= 10 \\\\[6pt]\n21x + 6y &= 30\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $x$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(x,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 2y &=10 \\\\ 21x + 6y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then we will get a $-21x$ term that can cancel with the $21x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 2y &=10 && \\mid \\cdot (-3) \\\\ 21x + 6y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-21x - 6y &= -30 \\\\\n21x + 6y &= 30 \\\\\n0 &= (-30 + 30) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 2y &= 10 \\\\\n2y &= 10 - 7x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{10 - 7x}{2} \\\\\ny &= 5 - \\frac{7}{2}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,5 - \\frac{7}{2}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e93e99b-7e76-59cd-a8bf-9d5a1e879a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e93e99b-7e76-59cd-a8bf-9d5a1e879a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542457} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f52dab6-f84a-51c1-bb5e-7609d7d43d80" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd33d3a8-634b-5300-83fe-512c3febb665" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x - y &= -4 \\\\[6pt]\n12x + 4y &= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $x$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(x,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x - y &=-4 \\\\ 12x + 4y &=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $4$, then we will get a $-12x$ term that can cancel with the $12x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x - y &=-4 && \\mid \\cdot (4) \\\\ 12x + 4y &=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x - 4y &= -16 \\\\\n12x + 4y &= 16 \\\\\n0 &= (-16 + 16) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x - y &= -4 \\\\\n-y &= -4 + 3x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-4 + 3x}{-1} \\\\\ny &= 4 - 3x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,4 - 3x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d56e4e-14df-5e76-8811-2258751260f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{7}{5}x - \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542450} {:answer/id #uuid "2b767e80-1eaf-555b-9465-6842cf1181fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{7}{5}x + \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542455} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdd62e8-0db4-5e13-9558-c017d95ac564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542478} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ea97ea-40ff-582c-b6e3-88f89d97fe8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{7}{5}x + \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542489} {:answer/id #uuid "c600e11f-1d2c-53ce-a422-159dac0d2e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{5}{7}x + \\frac{4}{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b767e80-1eaf-555b-9465-6842cf1181fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{7}{5}x + \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542455} :answer-field/id #uuid "986fd8e2-7152-5f37-bea8-d024be1e25a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fec9f06c-a4db-563f-96a3-164f1364ae78" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 5y &= 4 \\\\[6pt]\n-14x - 10y &= -8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 5y &=4 \\\\ -14x - 10y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $14x$ term that can cancel with the $-14x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 5y &=4 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ -14x - 10y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n14x + 10y &= 8 \\\\\n-14x - 10y &= -8 \\\\\n0 &= (8 - 8) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 5y &= 4 \\\\\n5y &= 4 - 7x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4 - 7x}{5} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4}{5} - \\frac{7}{5}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,\\frac{4}{5} - \\frac{7}{5}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "866eae0c-01b3-50bf-b526-86a0c6cac6c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561230} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa7f187-7fdf-5a83-ab02-69b55dfb828f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561244} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c3ac96-f810-55fd-8221-e27eafaa255a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "866eae0c-01b3-50bf-b526-86a0c6cac6c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561230} :answer-field/id #uuid "8500c6f6-dcab-5691-9d28-5480f89255f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a462c5e-dc46-5cbd-908d-8873a5836bec" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & y &{}={}& x + 6 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -3x + 3y &{}={}& 18\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= x + 6 \\\\ -3x + 3y &= 18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = x + 6\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=x + 6\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + 3y &= 18 \\\\\n-3x + 3\\left(x + 6\\right) &= 18 \\\\\n-3x + 3x + 18 &= 18 \\\\\n18 &= 18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75689f6e-65af-5364-b427-d0d53ea942af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561221} {:answer/id #uuid "79766299-4422-5446-8123-6c952ce516d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561225} {:answer/id #uuid "9eff61d3-41d1-56c6-bd82-959956a2ca75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79766299-4422-5446-8123-6c952ce516d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561225} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ec6e71b-2b03-5a5a-9cc6-7eb21d9e2203" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5c389456-1e7f-570a-b81d-ee3996221d09" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & 5x - 2y &{}={}& -1 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -10x + 4y &{}={}& 2\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x - 2y &=-1 \\\\ -10x + 4y &= 2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x - 2y &=-1 \\\\\n-2y &= -5x - 1 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-5x - 1}{-2} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-10x + 4y &= 2 \\\\\n-10x + 4\\left(\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}\\right) &= 2 \\\\\n-10x + 10x + 2 &= 2 \\\\\n2 &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9164734a-796f-5af8-ac94-62a22713d23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561234} {:answer/id #uuid "c60ae584-a9c5-5da2-b67b-9cea1d5ceb12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561246} {:answer/id #uuid "f5850239-8333-5a95-b556-84d53e0aa3e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9164734a-796f-5af8-ac94-62a22713d23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561234} :answer-field/id #uuid "8afb3dd7-ffd1-50e9-b1b9-598ad7c3ec84" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5dcff32d-252d-58bc-9fa9-cb87cd485a01" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & 2x - 3y &{}={}& 0 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 6x - 9y &{}={}& 0\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x - 3y &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 9y &= 0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - 3y &= 0 \\\\\n-3y &= -2x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-2x}{-3} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{3}x\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x - 9y &= 0 \\\\\n6x - 9\\left(\\frac{2}{3}x\\right) &= 0 \\\\\n6x - 6x &= 0 \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13da69cb-99ca-554d-8d6d-4260e2aaf8e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561195} {:answer/id #uuid "4417ae70-0890-5813-a5ad-6509930c237e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561206} {:answer/id #uuid "73ba1cde-65b2-5df1-8173-f771c3abe4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73ba1cde-65b2-5df1-8173-f771c3abe4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561220} :answer-field/id #uuid "49b90caf-daee-5b7f-adfd-50fdc0c131c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6542765a-dbf6-5f4b-aedd-6339210b9996" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -5x + y &{}={}& -1 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 10x - 2y &{}={}& 2\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x + y &=-1 \\\\ 10x - 2y &= 2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x + y &=-1 \\\\\ny &= 5x - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=5x - 1\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10x - 2y &= 2 \\\\\n10x - 2\\left(5x - 1\\right) &= 2 \\\\\n10x - 10x + 2 &= 2 \\\\\n2 &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28deb832-44b2-579c-bb80-e65dc4c0107e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561199} {:answer/id #uuid "6f64462a-0a21-5bfe-90c2-09bf574953ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561219} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4f350c-25be-5a95-b053-4cbb5ed6e773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561258 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574184}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb4f350c-25be-5a95-b053-4cbb5ed6e773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561258} :answer-field/id #uuid "087a9931-aed8-58f6-9406-32b8d1499065" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76b29f4c-d2f7-5be9-99e6-f351f6d667d5" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & y &{}={}& -5x - 5 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 25x + 5y &{}={}& -20\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= -5x - 5 \\\\ 25x + 5y &=-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = -5x - 5\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-5x - 5\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n25x + 5y &=-20 \\\\\n25x + 5\\left(-5x - 5\\right) &= -20 \\\\\n25x - 25x - 25 &= -20 \\\\\n-25 &= -20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9537567-1850-5466-995f-5f2a3e4745df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561243} {:answer/id #uuid "cb40c9bc-94bd-5b2a-ac25-2906284d6dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561251} {:answer/id #uuid "cdeed473-c033-56b5-80e0-c80a74ce7f4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdeed473-c033-56b5-80e0-c80a74ce7f4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561252} :answer-field/id #uuid "47b67ab5-2541-51b1-b6af-87cd3ee8f675" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "787cf7fe-f2f7-5df0-b36f-e78b6273a4b5" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -2x - 3y &{}={}& -4 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 12x + 20y &{}={}& 6\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x - 3y &=-4 \\\\ 12x + 20y &= 6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 3y &=-4 \\\\\n-3y &= 2x - 4 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2x - 4}{-3} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{2}{3}x + \\frac{4}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{2}{3}x + \\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12x + 20y &= 6 \\\\\n12x + 20\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}x + \\frac{4}{3}\\right) &= 6 \\\\\n12x - \\frac{40}{3}x + \\frac{80}{3} &= 6 \\\\\n-\\frac{4}{3}x + \\frac{80}{3} &= 6 \\\\\n-\\frac{4}{3}x &= - \\frac{62}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c788b1-e8d1-5ab2-b2ec-c639e5a5f429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561196 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574183}]} {:answer/id #uuid "78dd7c65-7c23-5532-976d-ff5e37ca8e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561224} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8afa02-2884-5634-93a8-7b7ccd61ae05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15c788b1-e8d1-5ab2-b2ec-c639e5a5f429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561196} :answer-field/id #uuid "486aff25-f9b1-5424-a420-03217a3f6814" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7990b398-b163-5ff0-bd59-3b73f685ea5d" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -4x + y &{}={}& 2 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -12x + 3y &{}={}& -15\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x + y &= 2 \\\\ -12x + 3y &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x + y &= 2 \\\\\ny &= 4x + 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=4x + 2\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x + 3y &=-15 \\\\\n-12x + 3\\left(4x + 2\\right) &= -15 \\\\\n-12x + 12x + 6 &= -15 \\\\\n6 &= -15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805cb854-3cef-5a9d-b52f-6cb5f1a05d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561228} {:answer/id #uuid "a3fd6325-a5dc-5571-807f-0a19cfc212a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561241} {:answer/id #uuid "f61301bd-60c9-56c5-bccb-3ea8e307b4a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "805cb854-3cef-5a9d-b52f-6cb5f1a05d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561228} :answer-field/id #uuid "c843a425-7cc2-5a78-8427-4b2970f00770" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96e99e9b-5b2e-55b0-8814-cc28b8bf6bc8" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -x - y &{}={}& 4 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -12x - 3y &{}={}& -12\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x - y &= 4 \\\\ -12x - 3y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x - y &= 4 \\\\\n-y &= x + 4 \\\\\ny &= -x - 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-x - 4\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x - 3y &=-12 \\\\\n-12x - 3\\left(-x - 4\\right) &= -12 \\\\\n-12x + 3x + 12 &= -12 \\\\\n-9x + 12 &= -12 \\\\\n-9x &= -24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d4a8325-79ab-5bbe-9c43-8395dff042e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561204} {:answer/id #uuid "ce74c59e-9e7a-5fcf-9bfa-74ca29a5dc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561253} {:answer/id #uuid "eeaec689-8e5c-5fbe-a829-38566863fd86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d4a8325-79ab-5bbe-9c43-8395dff042e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561204} :answer-field/id #uuid "d90c2268-eb7e-5503-ad73-e1ac5a2b2e15" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9a01d9c5-2885-5132-9235-1d9478baed14" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & y &{}={}& -x - 4 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -9x - 3y &{}={}& 15\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= -x - 4 \\\\ -9x - 3y &= 15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = -x - 4\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-x - 4\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-9x - 3y &= 15 \\\\\n-9x - 3\\left(-x - 4\\right) &= 15 \\\\\n-9x + 3x + 12 &= 15 \\\\\n-6x + 12 &= 15 \\\\\n-6x &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64762017-ef57-574d-99d7-a9be2892815d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561217} {:answer/id #uuid "8903af01-7bdb-59b7-bfc2-56796727445a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561231} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec78b20-d253-53dd-af36-f3b3e2a99e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64762017-ef57-574d-99d7-a9be2892815d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561217} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c7459c3-7647-57df-ac62-0f53b2bd604d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4be2362-89eb-587e-82aa-d9d4f04eb125" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -5x - y &{}={}& 5 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -20x - 4y &{}={}& -8\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x - y &= 5 \\\\ -20x - 4y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x - y &= 5 \\\\\n-y &= 5x + 5 \\\\\ny &= -5x - 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-5x - 5\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-20x - 4y &=-8 \\\\\n-20x - 4\\left(-5x - 5\\right) &= -8 \\\\\n-20x + 20x + 20 &= -8 \\\\\n20 &= -8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "303e264e-f7bb-58e1-8f43-28746c565777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561201} {:answer/id #uuid "f84d8eb6-0a3f-5c54-b516-d5072df2722e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561263} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1ddb6a-6d38-5bf0-ac22-13dff12c39f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f84d8eb6-0a3f-5c54-b516-d5072df2722e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561263} :answer-field/id #uuid "016fa648-d368-50d4-ab14-df62c0c4ad93" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c74e2f77-c144-59ff-a39d-154078a44e94" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & y &{}={}& 4x + 2 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -8x + 2y &{}={}& 6\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= 4x + 2 \\\\ -8x + 2y &= 6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = 4x + 2\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=4x + 2\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 2y &= 6 \\\\\n-8x + 2\\left(4x + 2\\right) &= 6 \\\\\n-8x + 8x + 4 &= 6 \\\\\n4 &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4da3fcc3-fa0d-5f01-ba15-7551732faeaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561210} {:answer/id #uuid "52d1d98a-2227-583b-995d-2d9f0f210a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561211} {:answer/id #uuid "e62ba3e0-8699-5115-910d-02ee319aed05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561256 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186656364}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e62ba3e0-8699-5115-910d-02ee319aed05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561256} :answer-field/id #uuid "43673130-deba-5b98-8ce2-b4ee4ed0101a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7e53da6-3b28-54ab-be32-bc2afa7301df" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & 5x + y &{}={}& -1 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -12x + 3y &{}={}& 3\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x + y &=-1 \\\\ -12x + 3y &= 3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x + y &=-1 \\\\\ny &= -5x - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-5x - 1\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x + 3y &= 3 \\\\\n-12x + 3\\left(-5x - 1\\right) &= 3 \\\\\n-12x - 15x - 3 &= 3 \\\\\n-27x - 3 &= 3 \\\\\n-27x &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cf58711-5f7d-5d0c-9c8b-5e45dbfc55fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561200} {:answer/id #uuid "57e75c5c-9d7e-5fbb-9e68-fd683aeb2452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561212} {:answer/id #uuid "ea88b994-5abc-51ab-a610-96e8bfe4ffaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cf58711-5f7d-5d0c-9c8b-5e45dbfc55fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561200} :answer-field/id #uuid "af3666b2-e413-595c-a093-783fa1dc8bf4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c878eb46-3c57-53bc-9b71-6029289efddf" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & y &{}={}& x \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -5x + 5y &{}={}& 0\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= x \\\\ -5x + 5y &= 0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = x\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=x\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x + 5y &= 0 \\\\\n-5x + 5\\left(x\\right) &= 0 \\\\\n-5x + 5x &= 0 \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561264 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32f19502-4a84-510e-96d9-21e50d95ed63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561202} {:answer/id #uuid "5d633272-a745-52f8-8022-869b2818e9f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561215} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d8f10b-db63-5f68-bb23-678f2810b48b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d633272-a745-52f8-8022-869b2818e9f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561215} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e4562de-6958-5910-a9b5-816e85d031d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f855e10a-f1b4-5356-9c10-ccedf77e81d7" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -5x - 2y &{}={}& -5 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 20x + 8y &{}={}& 21\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x - 2y &=-5 \\\\ 20x + 8y &= 21\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x - 2y &=-5 \\\\\n-2y &= 5x - 5 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{5x - 5}{-2} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n20x + 8y &= 21 \\\\\n20x + 8\\left(-\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{5}{2}\\right) &= 21 \\\\\n20x - 20x + 20 &= 21 \\\\\n20 &= 21\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561266 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e321ee9-c5ef-59e7-a720-449c297502e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561197} {:answer/id #uuid "96ad7a29-d44e-5997-8a2d-3dd126d93384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561235} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d98a33-6b71-5fc5-8f2b-3c8643f0ca6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e321ee9-c5ef-59e7-a720-449c297502e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561197} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fe7ee01-e7b5-51f5-a15c-7bbfebd4775e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe1a8df0-eeb5-5653-bde4-9ae932e3abc3" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & 5x - 3y &{}={}& 2 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 20x - 12y &{}={}& 7\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x - 3y &= 2 \\\\ 20x - 12y &= 7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x - 3y &= 2 \\\\\n-3y &= -5x + 2 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-5x + 2}{-3} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{5}{3}x - \\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{3}x - \\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n20x - 12y &= 7 \\\\\n20x - 12\\left(\\frac{5}{3}x - \\frac{2}{3}\\right) &= 7 \\\\\n20x - 20x + 8 &= 7 \\\\\n8 &= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23f644af-9084-5b6b-a224-bc40cc5bb33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640139} {:answer/id #uuid "7d2e874c-0781-5f71-b051-c295f819916f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640147} {:answer/id #uuid "b339515b-3078-5cfe-aea2-158ab2855c8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23f644af-9084-5b6b-a224-bc40cc5bb33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640139} :answer-field/id #uuid "d649dcd9-7ead-5b75-9f9a-f8c74e4bb08b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02757b3a-d6bd-5d7b-b6ab-661009ccee7e" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x - 8y &=-18 \\\\ -2x + 4y &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $2$, then we will get a $-4x$ term that can cancel with the $4x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x - 8y &=-18 \\\\ -2x + 4y &=9 && \\text{multiply by } 2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 8y &= -18 \\\\\n-4x + 8y &= 18 \\\\\n0 &= (-18 + 18) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=0$ is *always true*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nThe corresponding lines coincide."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640140 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ee12e6-4d64-54fc-aaa3-dc413abfc07c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640137} {:answer/id #uuid "59995b33-f05d-5fb4-8b50-2f0af671051f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640142} {:answer/id #uuid "7387d378-ae19-5bab-890c-24a374c27984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59995b33-f05d-5fb4-8b50-2f0af671051f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640142} :answer-field/id #uuid "1856f044-fcc3-5888-ba03-aa18503ab765" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3799138a-548f-5057-b762-ac999656fba6" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x - 10y &=-4 \\\\ 2x + 3y &=-14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $2$, then we will get a $4x$ term that can cancel with the $-4x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x - 10y &=-4 \\\\ 2x + 3y &=-14 && \\text{multiply by } 2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, the $x$ terms cancel, and we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x - 10y &= -4 \\\\\n4x + 6y &= -28 \\\\\n-4y &= (-4 - 28) \\\\\n-4y &= -32 \\\\\ny &= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x + (-10)(8) &= -4 \\\\\n-4x &= 76 \\\\\nx &= -19\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system has *a single solution*, $(-19,8)$.\n\nThe corresponding lines intersect at exactly one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ea58a8-b261-576d-9ccf-ce718b1a9fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640134} {:answer/id #uuid "5bea26c1-31ed-55d2-949c-1bbbde8ee93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640144} {:answer/id #uuid "d409007d-b812-5614-b531-fa9b6450b67b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08ea58a8-b261-576d-9ccf-ce718b1a9fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640134} :answer-field/id #uuid "236322db-7e50-5ad5-a390-389810077050" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f6c329f-7ffc-57d5-8497-a28129d7392e" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x + y &=-3 \\\\ -8x + 4y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $-4$, then we will get a $8x$ term that can cancel with the $-8x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x + y &=-3 && \\text{multiply by } -4 \\\\ -8x + 4y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8x - 4y &= 12 \\\\\n-8x + 4y &= -12 \\\\\n0 &= (12 - 12) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=0$ is *always true*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nThe corresponding lines coincide."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10067547-fcc2-5b8b-89ea-719c9b82856e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640135} {:answer/id #uuid "6db22fe2-6120-5dcf-b3d7-b07144ebf3cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640145} {:answer/id #uuid "f064ee3f-ed87-5f83-8fa8-8a24c01ee334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10067547-fcc2-5b8b-89ea-719c9b82856e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640135} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4181b34-dc50-52f5-bc34-ab88cbd2c0c3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59bf3201-eaad-59a1-ac3b-1b4fb93fe361" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x + 9y &=24 \\\\ -2x + 3y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $-3$, then we will get a $6x$ term that can cancel with the $-6x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x + 9y &=24 \\\\ -2x + 3y &=2 && \\text{multiply by } -3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-6x + 9y &= 24 \\\\\n6x - 9y &= -6 \\\\\n0 &= (24 - 6) \\\\\n0 &= 18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=18$ is *always false*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *no solutions*.\n\nThe corresponding lines are parallel and do not intersect."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2cb1eb8-0b50-5361-aa05-81b0dd19a4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640148} {:answer/id #uuid "c28146b0-299d-55a3-9f00-4faf5559f6e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640150} {:answer/id #uuid "fc6e06be-8ce6-59b7-88ed-17d453059107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2cb1eb8-0b50-5361-aa05-81b0dd19a4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640148} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1234034-2daa-59f9-ab64-b77c34f43090" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640156}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ee6ac6b9-b2da-5589-bfba-55b81fef39da" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x - 8y &=-8 \\\\ -2x + 4y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $2$, then we will get a $-4x$ term that can cancel with the $4x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x - 8y &=-8 \\\\ -2x + 4y &=4 && \\text{multiply by } 2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 8y &= -8 \\\\\n-4x + 8y &= 8 \\\\\n0 &= (-8 + 8) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=0$ is *always true*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nThe corresponding lines coincide."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5767e6ce-4cde-5db5-8f8c-d4de6b23f6ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640165} {:answer/id #uuid "57a4d089-fb9d-5bfa-8a19-7511789d5840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640166} {:answer/id #uuid "69ea3278-0545-57b3-83d5-aa2121cf9243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5767e6ce-4cde-5db5-8f8c-d4de6b23f6ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640165} :answer-field/id #uuid "df889c42-c3b2-5fc5-8775-cad2383fcece" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d131c71-5fda-5505-9c98-c1e16ef8f496" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & 3x + y &{}={}& 3 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 15x + 5y &{}={}& 10\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x + y &= 3 \\\\ 15x + 5y &= 10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x + y &= 3 \\\\\ny &= -3x + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-3x + 3\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n15x + 5y &= 10 \\\\\n15x + 5\\left(-3x + 3\\right) &= 10 \\\\\n15x - 15x + 15 &= 10 \\\\\n15 &= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1248c2d3-64d3-59be-b96d-926d2d600583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640160} {:answer/id #uuid "bdfdaf02-59b1-546f-b286-91313d3a3533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640175} {:answer/id #uuid "fc53ef36-fc6c-5fd5-8ce0-5ddb71ca4d4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1248c2d3-64d3-59be-b96d-926d2d600583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640160} :answer-field/id #uuid "af439d7a-b9a5-5085-bc69-012e5a130060" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20678e8b-456a-51a2-8a7a-d410f0c91f51" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -2x - y &{}={}& -4 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -4x - 2y &{}={}& -2\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x - y &=-4 \\\\ -4x - 2y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - y &=-4 \\\\\n-y &= 2x - 4 \\\\\ny &= -2x + 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-2x + 4\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x - 2y &=-2 \\\\\n-4x - 2\\left(-2x + 4\\right) &= -2 \\\\\n-4x + 4x - 8 &= -2 \\\\\n-8 &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4127f7b2-1111-52a3-b7db-c8518695824a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640164} {:answer/id #uuid "9a63b005-6c26-5d57-9323-8e05bd1b7f0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640172} {:answer/id #uuid "dabc714f-2415-5944-b6f0-d2ca3b986326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a63b005-6c26-5d57-9323-8e05bd1b7f0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640172} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea169a8a-5f68-598f-ad62-736a5366ad62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e5ef4b3-c03a-51cb-a9d7-c6314da020ef" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & 5y - x &{}={}& -3 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 10y - 2x &{}={}& 6\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5y - x &=-3 \\\\ 10y - 2x &= 6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5y - x &=-3 \\\\\n-x &= -5y - 3 \\\\\nx &= 5y + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\nx=5y + 3\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10y - 2x &= 6 \\\\\n10y - 2\\left(5y + 3\\right) &= 6 \\\\\n10y - 10y - 6 &= 6 \\\\\n-6 &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e467e83-433f-53b2-a85e-645cac8d5f65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640161} {:answer/id #uuid "322297c9-f6f7-5098-a2a8-0113f072d01b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640163} {:answer/id #uuid "985d1f73-cedf-53b9-8f5b-e5f6810c310c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "322297c9-f6f7-5098-a2a8-0113f072d01b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640163} :answer-field/id #uuid "8175714a-2aac-5262-8def-5d388c42e5a3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d8c99da-dd94-5d6a-a1d0-e2974f7c51cc" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -3y + x &{}={}& 5 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -15y + 5x &{}={}& 25\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3y + x &= 5 \\\\ -15y + 5x &= 25\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3y + x &= 5 \\\\\nx &= 3y + 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\nx=3y + 5\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-15y + 5x &= 25 \\\\\n-15y + 5\\left(3y + 5\\right) &= 25 \\\\\n-15y + 15y + 25 &= 25 \\\\\n25 &= 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3f7f2a0-106d-5608-9de9-2bd4e345f257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640176} {:answer/id #uuid "cc6703da-1178-576b-aecd-7d6f01eeeefe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640177} {:answer/id #uuid "f615e65d-ce7d-54e4-abde-94add209425b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc6703da-1178-576b-aecd-7d6f01eeeefe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640177} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2b8c4a4-cd52-5941-89f3-37b64c42ae72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1dcb86b-451f-5e07-9914-2cb09ff0199a" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -2y - x &{}={}& -6 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -8y - 4x &{}={}& -4\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2y - x &=-6 \\\\ -8y - 4x &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2y - x &=-6 \\\\\n-x &= 2y - 6 \\\\\nx &= -2y + 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\nx=-2y + 6\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8y - 4x &=-4 \\\\\n-8y - 4\\left(-2y + 6\\right) &= -4 \\\\\n-8y + 8y - 24 &= -4 \\\\\n-24 &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245912fe-e509-5c56-bae3-b0cca6df7fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640185} {:answer/id #uuid "744b8666-c1bd-5155-bdf6-f04f3bf98892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640187} {:answer/id #uuid "858335f2-e96c-54ee-b64b-3af41c61647e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "744b8666-c1bd-5155-bdf6-f04f3bf98892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640187} :answer-field/id #uuid "96630562-427d-5537-94eb-7d6bb432f4f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2696a764-12cb-5aae-b5d1-ef0ea644514a" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x + 2y &=-6 \\\\ 3x + y &=11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $-2$, then we will get a $-6x$ term that can cancel with the $6x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x + 2y &=-6 \\\\ 3x + y &=11 && \\text{multiply by } -2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x + 2y &= -6 \\\\\n-6x - 2y &= -22 \\\\\n0 &= (-6 - 22) \\\\\n0 &= -28\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=-28$ is *always false*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *no solutions*.\n\nThe corresponding lines are parallel and do not intersect."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5a4bb0f-9a43-5163-9697-12827dba7183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}x + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5a4bb0f-9a43-5163-9697-12827dba7183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}x + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640200} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ef280a6-0c78-5b88-9ee0-02b75b93c42f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f0547d1-fa31-5803-b06d-21be1313077c" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x - 2y &= -8 \\\\[6pt]\n15x - 6y &= -24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $x$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(x,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x - 2y &=-8 \\\\ 15x - 6y &=-24\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then we will get a $-15x$ term that can cancel with the $15x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x - 2y &=-8 && \\mid \\cdot (-3) \\\\ 15x - 6y &=-24\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-15x + 6y &= 24 \\\\\n15x - 6y &= -24 \\\\\n0 &= (24 - 24) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x - 2y &= -8 \\\\\n-2y &= -8 - 5x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-8 - 5x}{-2} \\\\\ny &= 4 + \\frac{5}{2}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,4 + \\frac{5}{2}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a7b7875-4d9b-5aed-9080-6e555d4af7fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}x + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a7b7875-4d9b-5aed-9080-6e555d4af7fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}x + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640199} :answer-field/id #uuid "7affe948-5e0e-5d3f-8148-757a9c9d15e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5de072c1-47a3-5741-ba9b-639b54a99874" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-10x - 3y &= -6 \\\\[6pt]\n-20x - 6y &= -12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $x$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(x,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-10x - 3y &=-6 \\\\ -20x - 6y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2$, then we will get a $20x$ term that can cancel with the $-20x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-10x - 3y &=-6 && \\mid \\cdot (-2) \\\\ -20x - 6y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n20x + 6y &= 12 \\\\\n-20x - 6y &= -12 \\\\\n0 &= (12 - 12) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-10x - 3y &= -6 \\\\\n-3y &= -6 + 10x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-6 + 10x}{-3} \\\\\ny &= 2 - \\frac{10}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,2 - \\frac{10}{3}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58a4801d-b268-5c08-abfb-e7c607ab165f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x + \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58a4801d-b268-5c08-abfb-e7c607ab165f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x + \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640194} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bc57d7e-ddc0-5363-ab23-525aff520425" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a7ee1c06-15eb-58c0-937e-df855179701b" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-6x - 3y &= -2 \\\\[6pt]\n-12x - 6y &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $x$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(x,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x - 3y &=-2 \\\\ -12x - 6y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2$, then we will get a $12x$ term that can cancel with the $-12x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x - 3y &=-2 && \\mid \\cdot (-2) \\\\ -12x - 6y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12x + 6y &= 4 \\\\\n-12x - 6y &= -4 \\\\\n0 &= (4 - 4) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-6x - 3y &= -2 \\\\\n-3y &= -2 + 6x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-2 + 6x}{-3} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2}{3} - 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,\\frac{2}{3} - 2x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "125c6f53-e126-5e46-9731-993fe4ab4b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "125c6f53-e126-5e46-9731-993fe4ab4b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640191} :answer-field/id #uuid "db744865-a71a-5972-986d-a77023f5db73" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640203}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b593e85c-2a9f-5880-abc4-b9008c8cc809" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x + 2y &= 1 \\\\[6pt]\n16x + 8y &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $x$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(x,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x + 2y &=1 \\\\ 16x + 8y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-4$, then we will get a $-16x$ term that can cancel with the $16x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x + 2y &=1 && \\mid \\cdot (-4) \\\\ 16x + 8y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-16x - 8y &= -4 \\\\\n16x + 8y &= 4 \\\\\n0 &= (-4 + 4) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x + 2y &= 1 \\\\\n2y &= 1 - 4x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{1 - 4x}{2} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{1}{2} - 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,\\frac{1}{2} - 2x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8522ac92-e497-558d-98b7-a8d6a3e5fad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{2}x - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8522ac92-e497-558d-98b7-a8d6a3e5fad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{2}x - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640198} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ec2b2b9-355e-581e-998b-3b7ce5e81395" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db879abc-a451-5b30-a7f1-852e57d16dee" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-11x - 2y &= 4 \\\\[6pt]\n-22x - 4y &= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $x$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(x,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-11x - 2y &=4 \\\\ -22x - 4y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2$, then we will get a $22x$ term that can cancel with the $-22x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-11x - 2y &=4 && \\mid \\cdot (-2) \\\\ -22x - 4y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n22x + 4y &= -8 \\\\\n-22x - 4y &= 8 \\\\\n0 &= (-8 + 8) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-11x - 2y &= 4 \\\\\n-2y &= 4 + 11x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4 + 11x}{-2} \\\\\ny &= -2 - \\frac{11}{2}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,-2 - \\frac{11}{2}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c56e158-ece3-5bbf-983b-287d761cfb1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640226} {:answer/id #uuid "b6cbda96-1fa4-51e0-b869-9b33dd471ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640228} {:answer/id #uuid "d5f2f498-fc15-5e76-8093-b7f43adcd507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6cbda96-1fa4-51e0-b869-9b33dd471ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640228} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dad72d3-9f99-5970-a5fd-2beeaefaad71" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0748cae-4d3d-5f93-a0a4-0643c8a9d6e6" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & x &{}={}& -4y + 4 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 16y + 4x &{}={}& 16\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &= -4y + 4 \\\\ 16y + 4x &= 16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $x$ in terms of $y$:\n\n$$\nx = -4y + 4\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\nx=-4y + 4\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n16y + 4x &= 16 \\\\\n16y + 4\\left(-4y + 4\\right) &= 16 \\\\\n16y - 16y + 16 &= 16 \\\\\n16 &= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54820552-1f76-578a-b822-cf2f98c93852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{10}{3}x - \\frac{5}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640238} {:answer/id #uuid "8616b1e3-87e5-502a-9f59-b051411cab84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{3}x - \\frac{5}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640239} {:answer/id #uuid "c472e356-bbfe-5d30-92ed-36f0bb018ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{10}{3}x + \\frac{7}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640241} {:answer/id #uuid "ca0a816c-0eb6-514f-9b62-d671cb280b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{10}{3}x - \\frac{10}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640242} {:answer/id #uuid "d71bf700-ea76-5013-b0b4-29a8c80b3fcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{3}x + \\frac{7}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c472e356-bbfe-5d30-92ed-36f0bb018ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{10}{3}x + \\frac{7}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640241} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3ce898a-eb93-55f0-b285-af50bbd97810" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a6c7666b-285c-575c-b0bc-ac496c8a866f" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-10x + 3y &= 7 \\\\[6pt]\n-20x + 6y &= 14\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-10x + 3y &=7 \\\\ -20x + 6y &=14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2$, then we will get a $20x$ term that can cancel with the $-20x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-10x + 3y &=7 && \\mid \\cdot (-2) \\\\ -20x + 6y &=14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n20x - 6y &= -14 \\\\\n-20x + 6y &= 14 \\\\\n0 &= (-14 + 14) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-10x + 3y &= 7 \\\\\n3y &= 7 + 10x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{7 + 10x}{3} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{7}{3} + \\frac{10}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,\\frac{7}{3} + \\frac{10}{3}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."}]
